{
  "$comment": [
    "The tournament ranking rule as executable cases. Read by BOTH suites - the Node tests in",
    "src/domain/tournament/ranking.test.ts and the JUnit tests in RankingEngineVectorTest - so the",
    "TypeScript and Java implementations cannot drift apart without a test failing.",
    "",
    "Order is WinPoint -> Diff -> Average Score, then head-to-head as a corrective pass inside a",
    "group already tied on WinPoint AND Diff. Average Score = scoreFor / games; a bye counts on both",
    "sides of that division, a penalty on neither.",
    "",
    "A meeting with winner:null is a draw. A meeting with penalty:true is not a game and must be",
    "ignored entirely. 'aggregations' is the number of FULL head-to-head aggregations the engine is",
    "allowed to perform - it pins the laziness requirement, not just the ordering."
  ],
  "vectors": [
    {
      "name": "WinPoint outranks everything below it",
